  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 36-layer alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 dielectric filter on fused silica substrate at 0 degree incidence, unpolarized light. Initialize all candidates to the baseline alternating profile: Ta2O5 layers at 43.0 nm, SiO2 layers at 180.0 nm, for 18 pairs (Air | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | ... | SiO2 | Fused Silica). Apply bounded uniform noise perturbation Δt ∈ [-5.0 nm, +5.0 nm] to each layer thickness during population initialization. Enforce hard bounds 20-350 nm on all thicknesses. Include a pairwise regularization term in the fitness function that adds penalty proportional to max(0, |t_i - t_{i+1}| - 30 nm) for each adjacent layer pair. Optimize for: maximum mean transmittance in 420-700 nm band, minimum mean transmittance in 355-365 nm band, minimum mean transmittance in 1030-1080 nm band, and minimum transmittance at 355 nm. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all valid candidates. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 6 alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 pairs (12 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 355-355 nm, 355-365 nm, 420-700 nm, 1030-1080 nm. soft objectives: high average transmittance in 420-700 nm; low average transmittance at 355 nm; low average transmittance in 355-365 nm; low average transmittance in 1030-1080 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance at 355 nm; high transmittance in 355-365 nm; high transmittance in 1030-1080 nm; high loss in 420-700 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 36 layers; layer thickness range 20-350 nm.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize continuous thicknesses for 12 alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 layers on fused silica at 0 degree unpolarized incidence. Maximize mean transmittance in 420-700 nm. Minimize mean transmittance in 355-365 nm, 1030-1080 nm, and worst-case transmittance at 355 nm. Enforce hard bounds 20-350 nm. Include ±5 nm absolute thickness noise in uncertainty analysis.",
